@startuml
title v0002-state-registry - historical record topology

participant "API Gateway\n(post-v0006)" as GW
participant "Executor\n(v0001+)" as Ex
participant "Operator /\ndirect caller\n(pre-v0006)" as Direct
participant "State Registry" as State
database "PostgreSQL\n(State Registry)" as Pg
participant "Router\n(post-v0004)" as Router
participant "Env Registry\n(post-v0003)" as Env
participant "Web UI\n(post-v0006)" as UI

GW -> State : state reads, control-request writes,\nevent subscription (WebSocket proxy)
Ex -> State : PUT /v1/executors/{id}, POST events\n(historical writes, control reads)
Direct -> State : GET task records, audit, events,\nPOST control-request records
State -> Pg : persist task records, task events,\naudit entries, control requests
State --> GW : task records, event stream, control records
State --> Ex : control-request records for assigned tasks
State --> Direct : task records, audit, control records

State -x Router : forbidden (no direct connection)
State -x Env : forbidden (no direct connection)
State -x UI : forbidden (UI talks only via API Gateway)

note over State
  Owns canonical task records, task event logs,
  audit trail, and operator control-request records.
  Does NOT queue, dispatch, hold env vars or secrets,
  or call the Router or Env Registry.
end note

@enduml
